WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.930
A US government-led study found that

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.310
2 in 3 patients said they understood the test results

3
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.950
viewed before talking to a clinician.

4
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.370
Now imagine the report itself changes.

5
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.870
Ferritin 5, and amended, is 50.

6
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.430
Same patient, same collection.

7
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.810
Which number should an AI say aloud?

8
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.010
Meet Voice Memory.

9
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.810
You ask. Bolna handles the speech.

10
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.470
Our evidence engine finds the original passage,

11
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.990
checks its status,

12
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.050
and sends back the answer the record actually supports.

13
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.810
Here, 50 is the corrected result.

14
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.950
Creatinine in different units,

15
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.950
without a validated conversion: no guessing.

16
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.730
And it goes beyond healthcare.

17
00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.450
A $48,000 offer becomes a $42,000 proposal.

18
00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.470
Still no finance approval.

19
00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.870
Meeting notes: discussed isn't decided.

20
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.370
One clear answer, its exact source on screen.

21
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.230
Voice Memory doesn't just find an answer.

22
00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:10.650
It checks whether the record allows that answer.
